+//! What a cluster costs: a model you can read a budget off.
+//!
+//! `meshkv/5.17-distributed-budgets` is the step where "it depends on the cluster size" becomes a
+//! number. Every write in this project costs a round of messages — the leader sends, a majority
+//! acknowledges — and every read at the linearizable level costs a round too (`5.6`). Those are
+//! **counts**, and a count is a budget: the same number on a busy machine as on an idle one, which is
+//! why this step's gate (`bench-budget`) judges counts and never wall-clock time.
+//!
+//! The model has three parts, and each of them is arithmetic a reader can check:
+//!
+//! * **the quorum.** `⌊n/2⌋ + 1` acknowledgements, because that is what decides anything in this
+//!   project (`5.5`, `5.14`, `5.15` all use the same number).
+//! * **the fan-out.** The leader sends one message per peer, so a write costs `n − 1` messages and
+//!   has to hear from `quorum − 1` of them. The two numbers are different and both matter: the first
+//!   is what the network carries, the second is what the leader waits for.
+//! * **the per-node share.** The leader sends one message per peer, so its work per write grows with
+//!   the cluster; a follower sends one message per write whatever `n` is. The average is therefore
+//!   `(n − 1) / n` messages per node per write: it *rises* towards one as the cluster grows, and it
+//!   hides the leader's `n − 1`, which is the number that actually scales. Stating both is what
+//!   makes this a budget rather than a diagram.
+//!
+//! Latency is counted too, in **hops**: a write waits for one round trip to the quorum, so its
+//! latency is one hop whatever `n` is; a *read* at the linearizable level is a round too. Nothing
+//! here is milliseconds — the moment a budget is a time, it is a budget that fails on a loaded
+//! machine (handoff M2 §1.1).
+
+use crate::error::Result;
+
+/// What one cluster shape costs for one write and one linearizable read.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct Cost {
+    /// How many nodes the cluster has.
+    pub nodes: usize,
+    /// How many acknowledgements decide anything.
+    pub quorum: usize,
+    /// How many messages the leader sends for one write.
+    pub messages: usize,
+    /// How many acknowledgements the leader waits for.
+    pub acks: usize,
+    /// How many round trips a write takes before it is decided.
+    pub write_hops: usize,
+    /// How many round trips a linearizable read takes.
+    pub read_hops: usize,
+}
+
+/// The cost of a cluster of `nodes` nodes.
+///
+/// # Errors
+///
+/// [`Error::Invalid`] when the cluster has no nodes: there is no quorum to compute, and a budget for
+/// a cluster that does not exist is a number nobody can use.
+pub fn cost(nodes: usize) -> Result<Cost> {
+    let _ = nodes;
+    todo!("meshkv/5.17-distributed-budgets: cost")
+}
